    The BatchNormalization fold is the entry worth staring at. TensorRT has no
    BatchNormalization layer, so the parser folds four ONNX initializers into two
    engine weights named tmp_refittable_weight*, using an epsilon that lives in a
    node attribute. Reproducing that by hand means re-deriving the parser's fusion
    rules and tracking them across releases. The observer just tells you.

